## Classification of “secret-looking” hits (not leaks)

These matched broad `secret_key` / hex greps but are **not** committed credentials:

| Class | Examples | Verdict |
|-------|----------|---------|
| Type / API fields | `SecretKey`, `client_secret: String`, `FheSecretKey` | library surface |
| Dummy verify padding | `"01234567890123456789012345678901"`, `"SUPER_SECRET_KEY"`, `"secret_key_pad"` | test/shim only |
| Keystore shim | `keystore_init(..., "password")` in `keys.oo` | pad, not operator secret |
| Curve constants | secp256k1 `p_hex` / `gx_hex` / `gy_hex` / `n_hex` | public parameters |
| Zero fillers | all-zero PCR / info_hash | placeholders |
| Filename false positive | `std/ai/tokenizer/` (BPE/WordPiece) | directory name, not auth token |

