## Root-cause notes (for DE / SPRINT T5)

1. **Secrets class is clean** — std is source-heavy with stub density; credential risk
   today is accidental future `git add` of local keys, not existing packed material.

2. **gitignore asymmetry** — ooda learned T4 secret globs after seed/signing work;
   org `std/.gitignore` never got the same hardening. Prefer proactive ignore parity
   before first operator signs anything under std.

3. **Honesty ≠ empty tree** — `process_exit` density is an intentional fail-closed
   residual for gated crypto/net. The load-bearing control is
   `std_honesty_t5_smoke.sh` refusing production-ready claims beside those gates.
   Do not greenwash density decline as “crypto done.”

4. **Cap-bypass scripts** — same debris class as T4; **absent** under both std trees.
   Keep absence as PASS; re-open only if strip scripts reappear.

5. **Two std trees** — `openOODA/std` (aspirational / broad) vs `ooda/std` (pure-path
   product). Security secret hunt covers both; product seal claims for FS/net/sys
   belong to `ooda/std` + runtime, not every untracked module under org std.

6. **Ship residual** — std is 20 commits ahead of origin; push/PR is T5 operator work,
   not this auditor.

