## What T5 secrets/supply path-A is **not**

> Absence of PEM/API keys in std is **not** a proof that every crypto module is
> constant-time or production-complete, **not** a seal that untracked files will
> stay secret-free forever, **not** gitignore parity with ooda, and **not**
> permission to claim sec/crypto is ship-ready while `process_exit` gates remain.

Re-open T5 security only if: (a) a real secret/key/`.env` lands in tree or index,
(b) cap-strip scripts appear under std, (c) honesty smoke fails on production-greenwash,
(d) binaries or signing private keys are tracked under std.

